    "sixtySeconds": {
      "whatItDoes": "Chroma is open-source data infrastructure for AI, best known as a vector database. You add documents with metadata to a collection, Chroma handles tokenization, embedding and indexing, and you query for the most similar results with optional metadata and text filters. It runs in-memory for prototyping, with persistence, or in client-server mode.",
      "problem": "RAG apps and semantic search need somewhere to store embeddings and look up similar text. Chroma does this with a four-function API.",
